+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+All six explanations and eleven ledger chains must be present; material
+conflicting values, alternative explanations and missing inputs must survive;
+source references must identify the physical page and acquired copy; preserved
+report/ledger bytes must match the native originals; only the listed new public
+files may be staged; every newly published agent-created commit must have the
+AveLyra author/committer identity; and the exact remote main commit and published
+file hashes must be checked after push. A local commit alone is not publication.
+
+## Preservation and disclosure boundary
+
+This is an original public-source research explanation with selected preserved
+research notes. Raw packet/OCR content and complete local acquisition/runtime
+files are not bulk-exported. The archived source-review manifest describes the
+native study's holdings, not this publication's file set. MANIFEST.json at the
+publication root defines this publication. No private case material, legal
+strategy, witness contact details, unredacted identities reconstructed from
+redactions, credentials or private keys are included.
+
+The earlier report's local/unpublished wording is deliberately retained as a
+historical snapshot. This record documents the separate later publication
+instruction. Updating that status by replacing its original text would conceal
+the sequence and is unnecessary.
+
+## Open work carried forward
+
